        "evidence": "t-from-trace-cyclicity.md:33-34 ('the reversed word produces the mirror-orientation link, which has the same Jones polynomial as the original by trace cyclicity')",
        "notes": "Word reversal of a braid β and Markov-trace cyclicity are distinct: tr_M(ab)=tr_M(ba) (cyclic rotation) does NOT give tr_M(β)=tr_M(β^T) (full reversal) in general — reversal is an anti-automorphism, not a cyclic rotation. The claim that the reversed-word link has the same Jones polynomial 'by trace cyclicity' is a non-trivial fact (true for these symmetric Markov traces, but it follows from the trace being symmetric/the Hecke algebra having a trace-preserving anti-involution, not from cyclicity). The stated justification is wrong even if the conclusion holds; as a conjecture this is softened to warn. Confirmed open: corpus carries this as conj:t-from-trace-cyclicity (open-problem tag), so flagging the cyclicity↔reversal conflation, not declaring the conclusion false."
      }
    ],
